email.body:
{{first}},

Our God's Special Children Christmas Party is on {{date 0}} in {{venue}}. Santa arrives around 3:00 PM, walks through the party, then sits in Santa's chair to hear each child's Christmas list, hand out gifts and take a photo that families take home.

Would you be our Santa this year? Please also let me know if you have a suit or need us to find one.

Tap here to answer: {{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Thank you again for preparing the Santa gifts. Last year we prepared 75 and gave out 42, so this year about 45 gifts should be plenty.

Please bring them to {{venue}} on {{date -1}} between 3:00 and 6:00 PM so we can set up the Santa station.

Tap here when the gifts are ready: {{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Please check our inventory so we have enough for about {{guests}} people. Check off what we already have, and reply or tap "I need help" for anything missing:

{{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Thank you for taking the Santa photos again. Last year you printed 40 Polaroid pictures of Santa with our GSC families (and donated the film - thank you!). This year please plan for about 45.

Tap here when you are set: {{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

The Sam's shopping list is ready. Quantities were adjusted from last year's leftovers (fewer buns, no chili, 10 lb of rice instead of 15).

Open the list and check items off as you shop: {{link}}

Please keep your receipts - you can upload a photo after the party for reimbursement.

{{signature}}

{{first}}, we are having a God's Special Children Mass and Christmas Party on {{date 0}} and will need the following:

1- Church's AC to be set to run from 1:00 PM to 4:00 PM.
2- Church's sound system left on after 12:00 PM Mass.
3- Both the front and back sacristies left open after 12:00 PM Mass.
4- {{venue}} unlocked at 11:30 AM.
5- {{venue}} AC or heater to be set to run from 11:00 AM to 6:00 PM, {{mdy 0}}.

Thank you for helping the Knights and Daughters host their annual God's Special Children's Christmas Party. As you know, our support for developmentally and intellectually challenged people and their families - these parties mean so much to them.

Please tap here when this is set: {{link}}

{{coord.name}}
{{org}}

{{first}},

Here is the jambalaya shopping list (Dorignac's, Restaurant Depot, Bailey's) and the propane refills. Per last year's note, only 10 lb of rice this time.

Check items off as you go: {{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Reminder: on {{date -1}} in the morning please pick up the buns at Sam's, as fresh as possible (latest best-by date):

  - 7 packs hamburger buns (last year 4 of 10 packs were left)
  - 6 packs hot dog buns (last year 5 of 10 packs were left)

{{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Reminder: we set up and decorate {{venue}} on {{date -1}}, 3:00 - 6:00 PM. Please remind your group.

Tables: 19 round tables (8 chairs each), 4 serving tables + 1 dessert table, Santa station at the front.

{{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Tomorrow, {{date 0}}:

  12:30 PM  Set up the cooking area, prep food, jambalaya, grill
   2:00 PM  God's Special Children's Christmas Mass
   3:00 PM  Christmas Party in {{venue}}
   4:30 PM  Break down and clean up

If you can, wear your council shirt.

{{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Before you leave the party, please count people and leftovers and fill in the results form. Every field is needed - it decides next year's shopping list.

{{link}}

{{signature}}

{{first}},

Thank you for all the shopping and cooking! Please upload a photo of each receipt (or just type the store and amount) so we can reimburse you:

{{link}}

{{signature}}
